The strategy has three parts. First, prefer moves that reduce the distance to the next unreached goal and are safe on every sensor: no patrol cell, no early goal, no obstacle arriving on the target, and no risky slip. Second, when no progress move is safe, take any safe sideways or wall-bump move, which lets the patrol's phase change. Third, fall back to progressively weaker safety conditions so every state is covered, ending with a catch-all. Because the rules use only the sensors and flags, not grid coordinates or `obs_idx`, the same list applies to every grid. I have not simulated the list on the grids, so the probability thresholds are not verified.

```json
{"rules": [
  {"condition": "toward & !wall & !patrol & !early & !risky & !obstacle", "action": "any"},
  {"condition": "!wall & !patrol & !early & !risky & !obstacle", "action": "any"},
  {"condition": "!patrol & !early & !obstacle", "action": "any"},
  {"condition": "!patrol & !early", "action": "any"},
  {"condition": "true", "action": "any"}
]}
```
